; Expect: Object does not exist
; The value of a field assignment is worked out before the object of the field is looked at, because a function of the program may let
; go of the last holder of a deleted object (which frees it). Storing into the freed memory would corrupt the heap; the program stops
; with an error instead, like for any other use of an object that is gone.
Type Child
	Field name$
	Field number
End Type
Type Parent
	Field child.Child
End Type

Global holder.Parent = New Parent
holder\child = New Child
Local second.Child = holder\child
Delete second ; Deleted, and held only by holder\child now.

Function Release$()
	holder\child = Null ; Last holder lets go, the Child is freed.
	Return "freed"
End Function

holder\child\name = Release()
Print "The freed Child was written to."
